# Copy to .env to run the mailer from your own computer with `npm run runner`.
# On GitHub these same names are repository secrets instead.
APP_URL=http://localhost:8787
APP_SECRET=local-dev-secret-change-me
# Several Gmail mailboxes, each sent through its own Brevo account's API. One array entry per
# mailbox: "user"/"app_password" are that mailbox's Gmail login (still used to read its
# replies/bounces — Brevo has no inbox of its own to check). "brevo_api_key" is that mailbox's
# own Brevo account's API key, from Brevo's SMTP & API > API Keys page (not the SMTP key).
GMAIL_ACCOUNTS=[{"user":"you@gmail.com","app_password":"aaaa bbbb cccc dddd","brevo_api_key":"xkeysib-aaaa..."},{"user":"you.backup@gmail.com","app_password":"eeee ffff gggg hhhh","brevo_api_key":"xkeysib-bbbb..."}]

# Alternative: a single Gmail mailbox instead of GMAIL_ACCOUNTS above (remove GMAIL_ACCOUNTS if
# using this). Sends through Gmail's own SMTP unless BREVO_API_KEY is also set.
# GMAIL_USER=you@gmail.com
# GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx
# BREVO_API_KEY=xkeysib-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
